# Core §15 — A HOST-LANGUAGE NAME IS AN ORDINARY UNKNOWN WORD.
#
# The refusal half of `960-prototype-names-as-ids`. Where the grammar wants a
# keyword, an enum value or an option key, `constructor`, `toString`,
# `valueOf`, `hasOwnProperty` and `__proto__` are words the language does not
# have, and each must get the SAME diagnostic any other unknown word gets
# there. Until this release the reference engine looked them up in plain
# objects: `shape=constructor` was refused with the text of a native function
# as its message, and `constructor a b` was called a keyword WITHDRAWN from
# this genre, with the same native text as the reason.
figdown 0.5 block
node a "A" shape=constructor
node b "B" shape=__proto__
constructor a b
toString a
__proto__ a
edge a -> b style=valueOf
edge b -> a hasOwnProperty=1
flow constructor
